## 5. MULTI-USER LIVE DATA SYNCHRONIZATION

When any authorized user creates, edits, approves, updates or changes a record, that change must be saved to the central SQLite database.

After the transaction commits, the central server must notify the relevant connected users.

Example:

```text
USER 1:
Updates Employee Department
        |
        v
Backend API
        |
        v
SQLite Transaction
        |
        v
Database Commit
        |
        v
Read-back Verification
        |
        v
Broadcast Change Event
        |
        +----------------------+
        |                      |
        v                      v
USER 2 SCREEN             MAIN HR USER SCREEN
Updates automatically    Updates automatically
```

Implement a reliable real-time update mechanism using the existing architecture where possible.

Options include:

- WebSocket
- Server-Sent Events (SSE)
- Existing reliable real-time transport

Choose the most suitable approach after inspecting the application.

Requirements:

1. Updates from User 1 must be visible to User 2 where permissions allow.
2. Updates from User 2 must be visible to the main HR/admin user.
3. Updates must appear without requiring a manual browser refresh.
4. Relevant dashboards must refresh when dependent data changes.
5. The current module and tab should remain open.
6. Avoid sending full employee or payroll datasets when only one record changed.
7. Notify clients which data changed, then retrieve the latest authorized record.
8. Reconnect automatically after temporary network interruption.
9. On reconnection, fetch the latest authoritative data.
10. Do not claim synchronization succeeded before the central database transaction is committed.

The main user's screen must receive updates regardless of which authorized computer initiated the change.

